  "rendered": "According to the document \"Tunable Mechanochemistry of Lithium Battery Electrodes\", the V2O5 film thicknesses tested electrochemically were 40 nm and 80 nm.\n\nTo determine the number of ALD cycles that gave the thicker film, we need to calculate the thickness of the 80 nm film. The document states that the thickness of the V2O5 coatings was estimated to be 0.07 nm per cycle. Therefore, the number of ALD cycles required to achieve an 80 nm film is:\n\n80 nm / 0.07 nm/cycle = 1143 cycles\n\nThe potential shifts were measured for both the 40 nm and 80 nm films, and the results are shown in Figure 4b. The figure shows that the potential shifts are similar for both films, with a mean red shift of ∼2 cm^−1 for the V−O1 (∼997 cm^−1) mode, ∼3.5 cm^−1 for the V−O3−V (∼483 cm^−1) mode, and ∼5 cm^−1 for the V−O2 (∼708 cm^−1) mode, and a mean blue shift of 1 cm^−1 for the V−O2 (∼303 cm^−1) mode. The results suggest that the potential shifts do not differ significantly between the 40 nm and 80 nm films.",
